Liliha Bakery, and afternoon tour includes a Musubi Platter from Iyasume Musubi\n\n#About\nView wild humpback whales and other diverse sea life in their natural habitat off of Oahu's stunning Gold Coast. Relax on our all-new double-decker boat with wrap-around bow seating in between whale sightings.\n\nWe begin with a powerful Hawaiian plumeria flower ceremony and chant, \"E Ho Mai\" to bring us good fortune during our voyage. We'll also serve up some morning beverages and pastries. Then we will cruise along Oahu's windward coastline in search of humpback whales.\n\nAs we begin to spot the whales, our crew will share information about their fascinating annual journey. If we are close enough, our crew will drop a hydrophone into the water to hear the whales' songs over our state-of-the-art sound system. Seeing whales up in person is an experience you will never forget!\n\nOn the way back you'll be entertained by our amazing crew. They'll perform authentic hula dance and songs. Don’t miss an opportunity to see one of the world’s largest animals in person during their migration through Hawaii!\n\nBook your tour today! Learn more [here](https://andyoucreations.com/whale-watching/)", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "Kewalo Basin Harbor Pier D: 1125 Ala Moana Blvd B1, Honolulu, HI 96814", "booking_notes": "#ALOHA,\nThank you for booking your **Whales and You** tour with [And You Creations](https://andyoucreations.com/).\n\nPlease read through this entire email for important general information regarding your tour. Don't hesitate to contact us if you have any questions or special requests.\n\nMahalo!\n_________________________\n#MEETING LOCATION\n\nTrolley transportation is available from three locations in Waikiki.\n\nFor guests who prefer to meet directly, please meet us at **Kewalo Basin Boat Harbor Pier D, Gate 111 ** [1125 Ala Moana Blvd D111, Honolulu, HI 96814](https://goo.gl/maps/gcpaNbTnFbA19to3A) (click on address for Google Map) no later than 6:45AM. Kewalo Basin Boat Harbor is 10-15 minutes from Waikiki.\n\nPublic parking is available but limited, and fees apply. If you plan to come by rental car, please arrive well ahead of your tour time to secure a spot. Uber, Lyft, and taxis are also available.\n\n**Please call 808-696-4414 for questions or assistance.**\n_________________________\n\n#WHAT TO BRING:\n• Sunscreen, Sunglasses, Hat\n• A light jacket for a cool ocean breeze\n• Camera / smartphone\n• Guests are encouraged to come in easily removable shoes or sandals.\n• Motion Sickness Medicine (For those who are prone to getting seasick, we recommend taking medication an hour before the tour start time)\n• Adult beverages will be available for purchase on the boat. Hard liquor goes from $6 to $12. Beer and Seltzers are $6.\n• Our meals do not accommodate allergies, We do not prepare the meals so we cannot guarantee anything regarding allergies. For your safety, please prepare your own.\n\nYou will be asked to remove your shoes before boarding the boat. This is for your safety. We will have storage for you to place them in during your time onboard. Clean reef shoes and grip socks are permitted.\n\nPlease limit your belongings to one bag per group due to limited space on the boat.\n\nIf you have a US number that we can reach out to, please contact us. \n\nSmoking, vaping, alcohol consumption, and the use or possession of illegal drugs are not permitted on our premises, including our buses and boats. Guests who do not comply with this policy may be denied service or removed from the premises at our discretion, without refund.\n\n_________________________\n\nGet ready to experience Hawaiian humpback whales in their natural environment!\n\n![Description of image](https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/CyLqmVRTXCMQNH14nYbg)", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "30% Off! with Code EB30 – Only in Winter! Witness the 